
Assessment
******************************************************************************
Section 2 — Infrastructure as Code
•	2b — Ansible (rolling broker config change)
==============================
In ansible/, provide a small role that:
•	Templates a change to server.properties (e.g., num.replica.fetchers=4).
•	Restarts brokers one at a time (serial: 1).
•	Before each restart, checks that under-replicated partitions = 0 and fails the play if not.
•	Does not restart brokers on a second run if nothing changed (idempotence).
•	Includes a short README explaining what it does and how to dry-run it.
We care about safety and idempotence more than YAML volume.
===============================
Answer:

ansible/
├── site.yml
├── inventory.ini
├── roles/
│   └── kafka_broker_config/
│       ├── tasks/
│       │   └── main.yml
│       └── templates/
│           └── server.properties.j2
└── README.md

task.yml

---
- name: Kafka rolling configuration update
  hosts: kafka_brokers
  become: true
  serial: 1

  roles:
    - kafka_broker_config

---
- name: Restart Kafka broker
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: "{{ kafka_service_name }}"
    state: restarted

inventory.yml

kafka_server_properties_path: /etc/kafka/server.properties

kafka_config_owner: kafka

kafka_service_name: confluent-server
kafka_broker_port: 9092
host:

kafka_server_properties:
  broker.id: 1
  num.replica.fetchers: 4
  log.dirs: /var/lib/kafka/data

kafka_healthcheck_host: localhost

